-- title:
--   Lemma 2.3 — non-explosiveness
-- statement:
--   Under Assumption 2.2 the increasing sequence $(\theta_i)_{i\ge1}$ tends to $+\infty$ almost surely. Furthermore, for any $r>0$,
--
--   $$
--   \lim_{n\to\infty}\sup_{(u,x)\in Q}E^{u,x}\big[e^{-r\theta_n}\big]=0,
--   $$
--
--   where $E^{u,x}$ is the expectation under the initial position $(u,x)$ for $(v,X)$ at time $0$.
--
--   This makes the process well defined for all times and gives the uniform decay that controls the tail of the series in (1.6).
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: bounded smooth domain → open, connected, bounded, with a global $C^\infty$ defining function $\rho$; reason: equivalent for bounded domains; the paper gives no degree of smoothness, read as $C^\infty$
--   - encoding: $f$ uniformly Hölder on $\bar Q$ with exponent $\alpha$ → Hölder for the metric of $\mathbb R\times\mathbb R^d$ with an existential $\alpha\in(0,1]$; reason: with $\alpha$ existential this and the parabolic Hölder class coincide on the bounded set $\bar Q$
--   - reading: $d$-dimensional balls, open or closed not specified → open balls; reason: the two readings agree, since $\varepsilon$ is arbitrary and balls can be slightly enlarged
--   - reading: measurability of $(t,x)\mapsto\nu_{t,x}$ with respect to the weak convergence topology → Borel for the topology of `FiniteMeasure` on $Q$; reason: this is the direct meaning of the phrase
--   - encoding: the process $(v,X)$ with $\theta_{i+1}=\inf\{s>\theta_i: X_{s-}\in\partial\mathcal O\text{ or }v_{s-}=T\}$ on a fixed filtered space → any `Realization`: the filtered space is part of the data, $\theta_{i+1}$ is the end of a cycle in $Q$ with left limit in $\partial_pQ$, stochastic integrals are `HasItoIntegral`, the conditional law is given $\mathcal F_{\theta_i-}$ with $\mathcal F_{\tau-}$ generated by the sets $A\cap\{s<\tau\}$; reason: same object: first hit written without an infimum of a possibly empty set; Mathlib has no $\mathcal F_{\tau-}$
--   - generalization: $\theta_i\to\infty$ from the initial position in $Q$ → from every real start time $t\ge0$ and clock start in $\bar Q$; reason: a start on $\partial_pQ$ adds one jump; the printed case is contained
--   - encoding: $\lim_n\sup_{(u,x)\in Q}E^{u,x}[e^{-r\theta_n}]=0$ → $\forall\varepsilon>0\,\exists N\,\forall n\ge N$, for all $(u,x)\in Q$ and all realizations from time $0$; reason: same content, with no real supremum over realizations
-- source:
--   Dai, Kou, Yang, A Stochastic Representation for Nonlocal Parabolic PDEs with Applications, SSRN 3541591, Lemma 2.3, eq. (2.13), p.9

import Definitions.Def_NonlocalFK_Realization

open MeasureTheory Set Filter

universe u

namespace NonlocalFK

/-- Lemma 2.3 (Non-explosiveness) (Dai, Kou, Yang, SSRN 3541591, p.9): under Assumption 2.2 the
increasing sequence `(θᵢ)` tends to `+∞` almost surely, and for any `r > 0`,
`lim_{n→∞} sup_{(u,x)∈Q} E^{u,x}[e^{−rθ_n}] = 0`, (2.13).

**Formalization Note.** `E^{u,x}` is taken under any realization with real start time `0`. The limit
of the supremum is written as `∀ ε > 0, ∃ N, ∀ n ≥ N`, uniformly in `(u, x)` and the realization,
which avoids a real supremum over realizations. The rate `r'` is the lemma's own. -/
theorem lemma_2_3 {d : ℕ} (m : Model d) (hS : m.Standing) (h22 : m.Assumption22) :
    (∀ t u : ℝ, ∀ x : E d, 0 ≤ t → (u, x) ∈ m.Qbar →
      ∀ (Ω : Type u) [MeasurableSpace Ω] (R : Realization m t u x Ω),
        ∀ᵐ ω ∂(R.P), Tendsto (fun i => R.θ i ω) atTop atTop) ∧
    ∀ r' : ℝ, 0 < r' → ∀ ε : ℝ, 0 < ε → ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ n ≥ N, ∀ p ∈ m.Q,
      ∀ (Ω : Type u) [MeasurableSpace Ω] (R : Realization m 0 p.1 p.2 Ω),
        ∫ ω, Real.exp (-r' * R.θ n ω) ∂(R.P) ≤ ε := by sorry

end NonlocalFK
